# Misjumps into witch space and fights the Thargoids there until they kill the commander. It starts from
# fighter.cdr (Tools/PrepareCommanders.py): the reference's own save, with Leesti selected, a military laser,
# ECM, an energy unit and enough kills (20) that enemies fire missiles. Alt+W during the countdown sets
# forceMisjump, the reference's own way to make a misjump; the arrival then puts the ship in witch space
# between the systems, where only Thargoids spawn, ten at once. The first spawns where the ship is (see
# mask-mission.replay: nothing has turned the spawn point yet) and dies ramming it; the military laser
# destroys another, each kill shortening the witch-space countdown; they launch Thargons, the ECM (E) removes
# the missile one fires, and they kill the commander: GAME OVER, then the title screen. The fight was played by
# a scratch program that steered at the nearest ship by its position every 50 ms, fired when it was in the sights
# and fired the ECM while a missile was out; what it pressed is recorded here like any other replay. It was flown
# again when the clock became milliseconds (D87).
file JAMESON.CDR fighter.cdr
wait 0.5; key space; wait 3.5      # any key: the credits, then the status screen
key Escape; wait 0.3               # the disc menu
key l; wait 0.3                    # Load Commander: it asks for a file name
key j; key a; key m; key e; key s; key o; key n; key Return; wait 0.5
